From 404dd7c99ca81e6fc980ab49e50fa9ba6c458dd0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.xyz>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:51:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] randd: seed from the BCM2835 hardware RNG (redox-rpi
 #556)

The Raspberry Pi 3B+ and Zero 2 W have no RNDR register, so randd seeded
with zeros and printed "Seeding failed ... NOT SECURE" on every boot.
Their SoC has a hardware RNG (brcm,bcm2835-rng, rng@7e104000). When RNDR
gives nothing, randd now finds it in the devicetree, maps it, starts it
with the warm-up count Linux uses unless the firmware already did, and
reads the 32-byte seed from it (at most 1 s, else the old message).
---
